      "id": "smoke-kafka-01",
      "technology": "Apache Kafka",
      "type": "identifier",
      "question": "What does the linger.ms producer setting do, and what is its default value?",
      "flags": [],
      "response": {
        "status": "answered",
        "reason": null,
        "answer": "The `linger.ms` producer setting allows the producer to wait for a specified amount of time before sending a batch of records, enabling batching of records that arrive between request transmissions. The default value is 5 milliseconds [C3].",
