      "id": "smoke-spark-02",
      "technology": "Apache Spark",
      "type": "how_to",
      "question": "How do I switch a Spark application to Kryo serialization?",
      "flags": [],
      "response": {
        "status": "answered",
        "reason": null,
        "answer": "To switch a Spark application to Kryo serialization, you can initialize your job with a `SparkConf` and call `conf.set(\"spark.serializer\", \"org.apache.spark.serializer.KryoSerializer\")` [C1]. This setting configures the serializer used for not only shuffling data between worker nodes but also when serializing RDDs to disk [C1]. \n\nFor custom class registration, use the `registerKryoClasses` method and pass an array of class references [C2].",
